{
  "requirement": "Each page has the same result fields as the originating tool. Text reads return\nsuccessive portions of text. Listings, outlines, and searches return successive\narrays of whole entries in their original order. Only a page with a successor\nincludes `next`.\n\nReusing a UUID returns the same page from the original snapshot, including the\nsame successor UUID if more remains. A malformed UUID, an unknown UUID, or a UUID\nfrom another conversation returns a tool error under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent.isolation`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The marked tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.pages.behavior`. I did not read the implementation. The one soft spot is that continuation paging is exercised only through `search_text`, not `search_structure`. I judged that acceptable because the checks on the shared page result fields would apply to both.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that check them**\n- **Text reads return successive portions of text.**\n  - `tests.rs#fn[graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change]` reads a multi-page node, changes the contents, then concatenates the page `text` values. It asserts they equal the original.\n  - `tests.rs#fn[source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read]` does the same for `read_source` line arrays.\n  - `project_sources.rs#fn[outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items]` does the same for root node text pages, with `file` and `selector` kept on each page.\n- **Listings, outlines, and searches return whole entries in their original order.**\n  - `project_sources.rs#fn[listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing]` uses 2000 files and a file added after the first page. The collected nodes equal the original ordered list.\n  - `project_sources.rs#fn[outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items]` checks the full ordered item list with node, file, selector and kind.\n  - `project_sources.rs#fn[search_pages_return_every_original_match_in_order]` runs after the file has been overwritten. It asserts every entry exactly, in order, and the total count.\n  - The `\"structural excerpt\".repeat(800)` check in `tests.rs#fn[source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results]` shows an oversized entry is delivered whole.\n- **Each page has the same result fields as the originating tool.** The outline test asserts `node` on every page. The search test asserts `complete`, `search_id` and `matches` on each page. The `tests.rs` read tests read `text`, `children`, `file` and `selector` on continuation pages. The listing test reads `files` entries.\n- **Only a page with a successor includes `next`.** The paging loops stop on a missing `next`, so a last page that carried `next` would fail them. `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` asserts `next` is present only on the first of two pages. The `pages > 1` assertions show the multi-page paths ran.\n- **Reusing a UUID returns the same page and the same successor UUID.** `pages.rs#mod[tests]/fn[text_listing_and_outline_continuations_replay_the_same_page_and_successor]` replays the second and third pages for text, listing and outline fields, and checks that the successor is present. The search test replays `get_next_page` at the end and asserts the text equals the earlier delivery after the source changed.\n- **A malformed UUID, an unknown UUID, or a UUID from another conversation returns a tool error.**\n  - The outline test dispatches `get_next_page` with `\"invalid\"` and with an all-zero UUID. Both must error.\n  - The unit test asserts a fresh `Pages` rejects an unknown id.\n  - The search test asserts a peer session's `get_next_page` errors on another session's `next`.\n  - `tests.rs#fn[graph_page_ids_from_a_populated_peer_conversation_are_rejected]` covers graph pages. It is the test for `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent.isolation`, which this requirement cites. I did not read its elided helper body, but it is marked and its name and assertions indicate the foreign-page check.\n\nThe `tests.rs` tests for `source_discovery_and_its_pages_do_not_register_reads` and `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` add checks on paging without re-reading or re-recording.\n\nThe cited isolation requirement is context only; I did not reassess its own tests.",
